{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":59,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.neg_logJet_c2_census","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.neg_logJet_c2_census","kind":"theorem","line":353,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L353-L361","doc":"The same for `−log`: still linear in the counts. The sign convention the bean\nasks about changes the sign of every term and creates no cross term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.logJet_c2_census","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.logJet_c2_census","kind":"theorem","line":334,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L334-L351","doc":"The census form: the type-two piece of `log` of the chain product is **linear**\nin `(n_pp, n_pn, n_nn)`, with no cross term — for `+log` (this statement) and,\nby `neg_c2`, for `−log`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.logJet_c2_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.logJet_c2_prod","kind":"theorem","line":314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L314-L332","doc":"**The `h²` coefficient of `log ∏ fᵢ` is `Σᵢ (cᵢ − bᵢ²/2)`** — per-factor, no pair\nterm. Compare `prod_c2`: the difference between the two is exactly `e₂(b)`, and the\nidentity that removes it is `sq_sum_eq`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.logJet_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.logJet_prod","kind":"theorem","line":303,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L303-L312","doc":"`log` of a product of unital jets is the sum of the logs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.logJet_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.logJet_mul","kind":"theorem","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L290-L301","doc":"`log (f·g) = log f + log g` on unital jets: the cross term `b b'` produced by\nthe product is cancelled exactly by `−(b + b')²/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.logJet_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.logJet_one","kind":"theorem","line":287,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L287-L288","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.logJet_c2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.logJet_c2","kind":"theorem","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L285-L285","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.logJet_c1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.logJet_c1","kind":"theorem","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L284-L284","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.logJet_c0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.logJet_c0","kind":"theorem","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L283-L283","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.logJet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.logJet","kind":"def","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L280-L281","doc":"The formal logarithm of a unital 2-jet, `log (1 + b h + c h²) = b h + (c − b²/2) h²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.smul_additive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.smul_additive","kind":"theorem","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L265-L272","doc":"Scaling preserves the Cauchy condition: `α • F` is additive when `F` is. So the\noverall energy scale (`E₀`, `α`, `m_e H_q(λ) u_λ`) never enters the shape question. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.neg_additive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.neg_additive","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L257-L263","doc":"Negation preserves the Cauchy condition: `−F` is additive when `F` is. So the\n`+log` and `−log` readings are one case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.additive_census","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.additive_census","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L246-L255","doc":"The census form of `additive_prod`: an additive functional of the chain product\nis **linear** in the three bond counts. Contrast `two_mul_e2_census`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.additive_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.additive_prod","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L236-L244","doc":"Under the Cauchy condition `F (∏ fᵢ) = Σᵢ F fᵢ` **provided** `F 1 = 0`. Every\ncoefficient of the image is then a sum of per-factor terms: there is no pair\nterm, whatever `F` is and whatever its sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.IsAdditiveOnProducts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.IsAdditiveOnProducts","kind":"def","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L231-L234","doc":"`F` carries products to sums — the Cauchy condition, and nothing more (the same\nhypothesis as `QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.IsAdditiveOnProducts`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.two_mul_e2_census","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.two_mul_e2_census","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L211-L227","doc":"The chain census: `n_pp` copies of the `pp` factor, `n_pn` of `pn`, `n_nn` of\n`nn`. The pair term is a **quadratic form in the three counts** with cross terms\n`n_pp n_pn b_pp b_pn`, `n_pp n_nn b_pp b_nn`, `n_pn n_nn b_pn b_nn`. Stated with the\nfactor `2` to stay over a ring (`C(n,2)` needs division). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.neg_prod_c2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.neg_prod_c2","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L205-L209","doc":"The pair term of the negated product is minus the pair term: flipping the\nsign convention (`+c₂` versus `−c₂`) does not remove the quadratic, it flips it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.prod_c2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.prod_c2","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L190-L203","doc":"**The pair term.** For factors with unit constant term,\n`[h²] ∏ fᵢ = Σᵢ cᵢ + Σ_{i<j} bᵢ bⱼ`: the bare type-two coefficient is the sum of\nthe per-factor type-two coefficients **plus the pair convolution of the type-one\nones**. This holds for `+∏` and, by negation, for `−∏`; the sign does not remove it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.prod_c1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.prod_c1","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L180-L188","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.prod_c0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.prod_c0","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L177-L178","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.sq_sum_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.sq_sum_eq","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L163-L171","doc":"`(Σ b)² = Σ b² + 2 e₂(b)`. This identity is what the logarithm uses to\nremove the pair term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.two_mul_e2_replicate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.two_mul_e2_replicate","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L153-L161","doc":"`e₂` of `n` copies of `b`: `2·e₂ = n(n−1)·b²` — quadratic in the count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.e2_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.e2_append","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L142-L151","doc":"**The cross term.** Splitting the factors into two classes (say the `pp` bonds\nand the `nn` bonds), `e₂` picks up the product of the two class sums — a product\nof two bond **counts** once each class is a repeated factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.e2_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.e2_cons","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L140-L140","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.e2_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.e2_nil","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L139-L139","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.e2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.e2","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L134-L137","doc":"`e₂ [b₁, …, bₙ] = Σ_{i<j} bᵢ bⱼ`, the pair convolution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.Jet2.isUnital_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.Jet2.isUnital_prod","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L119-L126","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.Jet2.IsUnital.one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.Jet2.IsUnital.one","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L117-L117","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.Jet2.IsUnital.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.Jet2.IsUnital.mul","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L112-L115","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.Jet2.IsUnital","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.Jet2.IsUnital","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L108-L110","doc":"The jets with unit constant term — the normalised factors `fᵢ/z₀`, i.e. the\nobjects whose `h²` coefficient is the probe's `c₂/c₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.Jet2.instAddCommMonoid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.Jet2.instAddCommMonoid","kind":"instance","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L101-L106","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.Jet2.instCommMonoid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.Jet2.instCommMonoid","kind":"instance","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L95-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.Jet2.neg_c2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.Jet2.neg_c2","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L93-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.Jet2.neg_c1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.Jet2.neg_c1","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L92-L92","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.Jet2.neg_c0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.Jet2.neg_c0","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L91-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.Jet2.zero_c2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.Jet2.zero_c2","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L90-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.Jet2.zero_c1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.Jet2.zero_c1","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GradedBindingFunctionalPairTerm.lean#L89-L89"